        {
          "@id": "urn:uuid:1a4956a8-f5d6-5234-9b7d-588974e008f7",
          "@type": "uco-observable:ExtractedStringsFacet",
          "uco-observable:strings": [
            {
              "@id": "urn:uuid:20e7fdbc-6552-53b8-a429-9166010dc3d6",
              "@type": "uco-observable:ExtractedString",
              "uco-observable:stringValue": "I\n\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS\n,/\nDocument 1 Filed 08/24/23 Page 1 of 5 PageID.1\n\nCLARE E. CONNORS #7936 \u25a011llll\nUnited States Attorney\nDistrict of Hawaii FILED IN THE\nUNITED STATES DISTRICT COURT\nREBECCA A. PERLMUTTER DISTRICT OF HAWAII\nAssistant United States Attorney AUG 2 11 2023 a,1\nRoom 6-100, PJKK Federal Building\nat l ~'clock and 4o minf__M\n300 Ala Moana Boulevard Lucy H. Carrfllo, Clerk\nHonolulu, Hawaii 96850\nTelephone: (808) 541-2850\nFax: (808) 541-2958\nEmail: Rebecca.Perlmutter@usdoj.gov\n\nAttorneys for Plaintiff\nUNITED STATES OF AMERICA\n\nIN THE UNITED STATES DISTRICT COURT\n\nFOR THE DISTRICT OF HAWAll\n\nUNITED STATES OF AMERICA,\n) CR. NO. 23- C(ff 2 3 - O\u00b7t0,0 7 1 JMS\n)\nPlaintiff, ) INDICTMENT\n)\nvs. ) [18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 225l(a), 2252(a)(4)(B)]\n)\nDARREN PATRICK RILEY, )\n)\nDefendant. )\n_ _ _ _ _ _ _ __ )\nINDICTMENT\n\nThe Grand Jury charges:\n\\\\\n\n\\\\\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 1 Filed 08/24/23 Page 2 of 5 PageID.2\n\nCOUNTl\nProduction of Child Pornography\n(18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2251(a))\n\nIn or around summer 2019, within the District of Hawaii and elsewhere,\n\nDARREN PATRICK RILEY, the defendant, did attempt to and did employ, use,\n\npersuade, induce, entice, and coerce a minor to engage in sexually explicit conduct\n\nfor the purpose of producing any visual depiction of such conduct, knowing and\n\nhaving reason to know that any such visual depiction would be transported and\n\ntransmitted using any means and facility of interstate and foreign commerce and in\n\nand affecting such commerce, and where any visual depiction was produced using\n\nmaterials that had been mailed, shipped, and transported in and affecting interstate\n\nand foreign commerce by any means, including by computer, and where any such\n\nvisual depiction was actually transp01ied and transmitted using any means and\n\nfacility of interstate and foreign commerce and in and affecting such commerce.\n\nAll in violation of Title 18, United States Code, Section 2251(a).\n\nCOUNT2\nPossession of Child Pornography\n(18 U.S.C. \u00a7\u00a7 2252(a)(4), (b)(2))\n\nOn or about December 14, 2022, within the District of Hawaii and\n\nelsewhere, DARREN PATRICK RILEY, the defendant, did unlawfully and\n\nknowingly possess a matter that contained images of visual depictions of minors\n\nengaged in sexually explicit conduct, including prepubescent minors and minors\n\n2\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 1 Filed 08/24/23 Page 3 of 5 PageID.3\n\nwho had not attained 12 years of age, with RILEY then knowing that said images\n\ncontained visual depictions involved the use of minors engaged in sexually explicit\n\nconduct, including prepubescent minors and minors who had not attained 12 years\n\nof age, and which depictions were of such conduct, had been transported in\n\ninterstate and foreign commerce, and had been produced using materials which had\n\nbeen mailed, shipped, and transported in interstate and foreign commerce.\n\nAll in violation of Title 18, United States Code, Sections 2252(a)( 4)(B) and\n\n2252(b)(2).\n\nFORFEITURE NOTICE\n\n1. The allegations in this Information are incorporated here for the\n\npurpose of noticing forfeitures pursuant to Title 18, United States Code, Section\n\n2253.\n\n2. The United States hereby gives notice to DARREN PATRICK RILEY,\n\nthe defendant, that, upon conviction of an offense in violation of Title 18, United\n\nStates Code, Section 2251, the United States will seek forfeiture, in accordance with\n\nTitle 18, United States Code, Section 2253, of (a) any visual depiction described in\n\nTitle 18, United States Code, Section 2252, and any book, magazine, periodical,\n\nfilm, videotape, or other matter which contains any such visual depiction, which was\n\nproduced, transported, mailed, shipped, or received in violation of that section; (b)\n\nany property, real or personal, constituting or traceable to gross profits or other\n\n3\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 1 Filed 08/24/23 Page 4 of 5 PageID.4\n\nproceeds obtained from such offense; and (c) any property, real or personal, used or\n\nintended to be used to commit or to promote the commission of such offense or any\n\nproperty traceable to such property.\n\n3. If by any act or omission of the defendant, any of the property subject\n\nto forfeiture described in paragraph 2 herein:\n\na. cannot be located upon the exercise of due diligence;\n\nb. has been transferred or sold to, or deposited with, a third party;\n\nc. has been placed beyond the jurisdiction of the court;\n\nd. has been substantially diminished in value; or\n\n\\\\\n\n\\\\\n\n\\\\\n\n\\\\\n\n4\nCase 1:23-cr-00071-JMS Document 1 Filed 08/24/23 Page 5 of 5 PageID.5\n\ne. has been commingled with other property which cannot be subdivided\n\nwithout difficulty, the United States will be entitled to forfeiture of substitute\n\nproperty up to the value of the prope1ty described above in paragraph 2, pursuant\n\nto Title 21 , United States Code, Section 853(p), as incorporated by Title 18, United\n\nStates Code, Section 2253.\n\nDATED: August ~~!D, 2023, at Honolulu, Hawaii.\n\nls/Foreperson\nGRAND JURY FOREPERSON\n\nCLA\nUnited States Attorney\nDistrict of Hawaii\n\n~~o~\nREBECCA A. PERLMUTTER\nAssistant U.S . Atto1ney\n\nUn~ted States v. Dan-en Patrick Riley, C~. ~~23-\n'R\nIndictment C 2 3 _ Q-0 Q 7 1 J:t\\J:i~\n5"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
